id":"g58JEMxrssPR","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786953250590,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":174,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"bb352f2d-27b2-485d-c315-45666235f986"},"execution_count":3,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["d/dx (x**2) = 2*x\n","Symbolic f'(3) = 6\n"]}],"source":["# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","# 🔹 1B. SYMBOLIC DERIVATIVE (SymPy)\n","# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","\n","expr = x**2\n","deriv = sp.diff(expr, x)          # differentiate w.r.t. x\n","print('d/dx (x**2) =', deriv)     # 2*x\n","\n","# Evaluate the symbolic derivative at x = 3\n","print('Symbolic f\\'(3) =', deriv.subs(x, 3))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"5O3gIB21ssPR"},"source":["#### 🧪 LAB EXERCISE 1 — Numerical vs symbolic derivative\n","\n","For the function `g(x) = x**3 + 2*x`:\n","1. Compute the **numerical** derivative at `x = 2` using a finite difference.\n","2. Compute the **symbolic** derivative with `sp.diff` and print it.\n","3. Evaluate the symbolic derivative at `x = 2` and confirm it matches step 1."]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def g(x):\n","    return x**3 + 2*x\n","\n","# 1. Numerical derivative at x = 2 (use h = 1e-6)\n","x = 2\n","h = 1e-6\n","numerical_derivative = (g(x + h) - g(x)) / h\n","print(\"Numerical derivative:\", numerical_derivative)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"kobucxQ3uUQt","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786953464805,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":43,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"7ad99b04-0272-4936-df1d-a415bfcf4955"},"execution_count":5,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Numerical derivative: 14.000006002490295\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","# 2. Symbolic derivative of x**3 + 2*x\n","import sympy as sp\n","\n","x_sym = sp.Symbol('x')\n","g_sym = x_sym**3 + 2*x_sym\n","symbolic_derivative = sp.diff(g_sym, x_sym)\n","print(\"Symbolic derivative:\", symbolic_derivative)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"rH64imv7umH0","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786953505179,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":10,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"d8983064-cfaf-4ed3-f4fc-4f65d5f064d7"},"execution_count":6,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Symbolic derivative: 3*x**2 + 2\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# 3. Evaluate the symbolic derivative at x = 2 and compare\n","symbolic_at_2 = symbolic_derivative.subs(x_sym, 2)\n","print(\"Symbolic derivative at x=2:\", symbolic_at_2)\n","print(\"Match:\", abs(numerical_derivative - float(symbolic_at_2)) < 1e-5)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"x9CfLYDxutuM","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786953524957,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":15,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"7e767a0c-272d-48a5-f0f0-c3be6062acf9"},"execution_count":7,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Symbolic derivative at x=2: 14\n","Match: True\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"A0YvvCdlssPS"},"source":["#2. Partial derivatives & the gradient"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import sympy as sp\n","\n","x_sym, y_sym = sp.symbols('x y')\n","\n","f2 = x_sym**2 + 3*x_sym*y_sym + y_sym**2\n","\n","# Partial derivative with respect to x\n","print('df/dx =', sp.diff(f2, x_sym))\n","\n","# Partial derivative with respect to y\n","print('df/dy =', sp.diff(f2, y_sym))"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"xImCoEcTvErN","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786953819218,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":46,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"5aa74b29-0156-428f-eeb9-443e00f03a92"},"execution_count":13,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["df/dx = 2*x + 3*y\n","df/dy = 3*x + 2*y\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"Qbsp-P9HssPS","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786953819782,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":12,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"50a01cd8-d98c-47e7-9b7f-653bff1c3dd1"},"execution_count":14,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["grad f = [2*x + 3*y, 3*x + 2*y]\n","grad f at (1, 2) = [8, 7]\n"]}],"source":["# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","# 🔹 2B. THE GRADIENT (vector of partials)\n","# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","\n","# The gradient stacks every partial derivative into one vector\n","grad = [sp.diff(f2, v) for v in (x_sym, y_sym)]\n","print('grad f =', grad)\n","\n","# Evaluate the gradient at the point (x=1, y=2)\n","grad_at = [g.subs({x_sym: 1, y_sym: 2}) for g in grad]\n","print('grad f at (1, 2) =', grad_at)   # points in the steepest-ascent direction"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"7IbSCkW8ssPS"},"source":["#### 🧪 LAB EXERCISE 2 — Compute a gradient\n","\n","For `h2 = x**2 * y + sp.sin(y)`:\n","1. Compute `dh/dx` and `dh/dy` with `sp.diff`.\n","2. Assemble the gradient as a list `[dh/dx, dh/dy]`.\n","3. Evaluate the gradient at the point `(x=2, y=0)`."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"RAQBcyNYssPS","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786953855902,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":5,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"e3784cae-e312-4b46-cd4f-29330327fde3"},"execution_count":16,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["dh/dx = 2*x*y\n","dh/dy = x**2 + cos(y)\n","grad h2 = [2*x*y, x**2 + cos(y)]\n","grad h2 at (2, 0) = [0, 5]\n"]}],"source":["h2 = x_sym**2 * y_sym + sp.sin(y_sym)\n","\n","# 1. dh/dx and dh/dy\n","dh_dx = sp.diff(h2, x_sym)\n","dh_dy = sp.diff(h2, y_sym)\n","print('dh/dx =', dh_dx)\n","print('dh/dy =', dh_dy)\n","\n","# 2. Assemble the gradient list\n","grad_h2 = [dh_dx, dh_dy]\n","print('grad h2 =', grad_h2)\n","\n","# 3. Evaluate at (x=2, y=0)\n","grad_h2_at_2_0 = [g.subs({x_sym: 2, y_sym: 0}) for g in grad_h2]\n","print('grad h2 at (2, 0) =', grad_h2_at_2_0)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"uyRBWemPssPS"},"source":["#3. The chain rule"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"foM7l_2wssPT","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786953918539,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":5,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"2c000788-1c4d-47e2-c5fe-419c4235217d"},"execution_count":19,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["By hand : 2*x*cos(x**2)\n","By SymPy: 2*x*cos(x**2)\n","Match?   True\n"]}],"source":["# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","# 🔹 3A. CHAIN RULE BY HAND vs SymPy\n","# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","\n","# y = sin(x_sym**2) is a composition: outer = sin(u), inner = u = x_sym**2\n","# Chain rule:  dy/dx = cos(u) * du/dx = cos(x_sym**2) * 2*x_sym\n","by_hand = sp.cos(x_sym**2) * 2*x_sym\n","by_sympy = sp.diff(sp.sin(x_sym**2), x_sym)\n","\n","print('By hand :', by_hand)\n","print('By SymPy:', by_sympy)\n","print('Match?  ', sp.simplify(by_hand - by_sympy) == 0)"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"iTlNtOeFssPT","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786953955216,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":7,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"7039fc81-ea88-4281-a84b-24bb6cb2619d"},"execution_count":21,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["d/dx (3x+1)^4 = 12*(3*x + 1)**3\n"]}],"source":["# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","# 🔹 3B. CHAINING THREE FUNCTIONS\n","# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","\n","# y = (3x + 1)**4  -> outer^4, inner (3x+1)\n","expr3 = (3*x_sym + 1)**4\n","print('d/dx (3x+1)^4 =', sp.diff(expr3, x_sym))   # 12*(3x+1)^3"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"lP13gePdssPT"},"source":["#### 🧪 LAB EXERCISE 3 — Chain rule\n","\n","For `y = sp.exp(x**2 + 1)`:\n","1. Write the chain-rule result **by hand** as a SymPy expression (outer derivative × inner derivative).\n","2. Differentiate the same expression with `sp.diff`.\n","3. Confirm the two match using `sp.simplify(by_hand - by_sympy) == 0`."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"saB9Jp_xssPT"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["# y = exp(x**2 + 1);  inner = x**2 + 1, inner' = 2x, outer' = exp(inner)\n","\n","# 1. By hand (as a SymPy expression)\n","# YOUR CODE HERE\n","\n","# 2. With sp.diff\n","# YOUR CODE HERE\n","\n","# 3. Confirm they match\n","# YOUR CODE HERE"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# y = exp(x**2 + 1); inner = x**2 + 1, inner' = 2*x, outer' = exp(inner)\n","\n","y = sp.exp(x_sym**2 + 1)\n","\n","# 1. By hand: outer derivative * inner derivative\n","by_hand = sp.exp(x_sym**2 + 1) * (2*x_sym)\n","print(\"By hand:\", by_hand)\n","\n","# 2. With sp.diff\n","by_sympy = sp.diff(y, x_sym)\n","print(\"With SymPy:\", by_sympy)\n","\n","# 3. Confirm they match\n","print(\"Match:\", sp.simplify(by_hand - by_sympy) == 0)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"G_Q1SjNVwkiu","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786954028721,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":13,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"63516e84-898f-433b-e62d-eca5cd544d4a"},"execution_count":23,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["By hand: 2*x*exp(x**2 + 1)\n","With SymPy: 2*x*exp(x**2 + 1)\n","Match: True\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"FVvOh5iIssPT"},"source":["#4. Backpropagation — the chain rule in a network\n","\n","A 2-layer network is just a composition:  **x → (W1) → ReLU → (W2) → y_hat**. Backprop applies the chain rule from the loss backwards to every weight."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"dSbLT6ZCssPT","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786954047536,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":16,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"7bd20fde-53e0-4963-d335-d26dae0d7135"},"execution_count":24,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Initial loss: 1.6936\n"]}],"source":["# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","# 🔹 4A. FORWARD PASS\n","# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","\n","# Tiny toy problem: 4 samples, 3 input features, 5 hidden units, 1 output\n","X = np.random.randn(4, 3)\n","Y = np.random.randn(4, 1)\n","W1 = np.random.randn(3, 5) * 0.1\n","W2 = np.random.randn(5, 1) * 0.1\n","\n","z1 = X @ W1                 # linear layer 1\n","h  = np.maximum(0, z1)      # ReLU activation\n","y_hat = h @ W2              # linear layer 2 (prediction)\n","loss = ((y_hat - Y) ** 2).mean()\n","print('Initial loss:', round(loss, 4))"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"WnQsUUcTssPT","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786954058984,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":346,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"3dbb7e26-a398-4332-8408-9cb8398691ad"},"execution_count":25,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["dW1 shape: (3, 5) (matches W1)\n","dW2 shape: (5, 1) (matches W2)\n"]}],"source":["# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","# 🔹 4B. BACKWARD PASS (gradients via the chain rule)\n","# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","\n","# Work backwards from the loss, one link at a time\n","dy   = 2 * (y_hat - Y) / Y.size      # d loss / d y_hat\n","dW2  = h.T @ dy                      # d loss / d W2\n","dh   = dy @ W2.T                     # d loss / d h\n","dz1  = dh * (z1 > 0)                 # ReLU gradient (1 where z1>0 else 0)\n","dW1  = X.T @ dz1                     # d loss / d W1\n","\n","print('dW1 shape:', dW1.shape, '(matches W1)')\n","print('dW2 shape:', dW2.shape, '(matches W2)')"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"7eKTlXc-ssPU","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786954070163,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":13,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"11b2804d-9bd6-4e73-d238-3efcf75b6d6e"},"execution_count":26,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Loss before: 1.6936\n","Loss after : 1.6524 -> should be lower\n"]}],"source":["# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","# 🔹 4C. ONE GRADIENT-DESCENT STEP SHOULD LOWER THE LOSS\n","# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","\n","lr = 0.1\n","W1 -= lr * dW1               # step downhill\n","W2 -= lr * dW2\n","\n","# Recompute the loss after the update\n","h_new = np.maximum(0, X @ W1)\n","loss_new = ((h_new @ W2 - Y) ** 2).mean()\n","print('Loss before:', round(loss, 4))\n","print('Loss after :', round(loss_new, 4), '-> should be lower')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"pdusVgqissPU"},"source":["#### 🧪 LAB EXERCISE 4 — Derive the gradients for a 2-layer network\n","\n","Fresh weights are set up below. Using the chain rule (reuse the pattern from 4A/4B):\n","1. Run the **forward pass**: compute `z1`, `h` (ReLU), `y_hat`, and `loss`.\n","2. Run the **backward pass**: compute `dy`, `dW2`, `dh`, `dz1`, `dW1`.\n","3. Take one gradient-descent step (`lr = 0.05`) and print the loss before and after."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"CQ8VvctussPU"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["Xb = np.random.randn(6, 4)\n","Yb = np.random.randn(6, 1)\n","Wa = np.random.randn(4, 8) * 0.1     # input -> hidden\n","Wb = np.random.randn(8, 1) * 0.1     # hidden -> output\n","\n","# 1. Forward pass: z1, h = ReLU(z1), y_hat, loss\n","# YOUR CODE HERE\n","\n","# 2. Backward pass: dy, dWb, dh, dz1, dWa\n","# YOUR CODE HERE\n","\n","# 3. One step with lr = 0.05; print loss before and after\n","# YOUR CODE HERE"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["Xb = np.random.randn(6, 4)\n","Yb = np.random.randn(6, 1)\n","Wa = np.random.randn(4, 8) * 0.1     # input -> hidden\n","Wb = np.random.randn(8, 1) * 0.1     # hidden -> output\n","\n","# 1. Forward pass\n","z1 = Xb @ Wa\n","h = np.maximum(0, z1)                # ReLU\n","y_hat = h @ Wb\n","loss = np.mean((y_hat - Yb)**2)\n","\n","print(\"Loss before:\", loss)\n","\n","# 2. Backward pass\n","dy = 2 * (y_hat - Yb) / Yb.size\n","\n","dWb = h.T @ dy\n","\n","dh = dy @ Wb.T\n","\n","# ReLU derivative: 1 where z1 > 0, otherwise 0\n","dz1 = dh * (z1 > 0)\n","\n","dWa = Xb.T @ dz1\n","\n","# 3. One gradient-descent step\n","lr = 0.05\n","\n","Wa -= lr * dWa\n","Wb -= lr * dWb\n","\n","# Forward pass again to calculate new loss\n","z1 = Xb @ Wa\n","h = np.maximum(0, z1)\n","y_hat = h @ Wb\n","loss_after = np.mean((y_hat - Yb)**2)\n","\n","print(\"Loss after:\", loss_after)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"8CFijaWTxBS9","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786954130918,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":38,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"28ad8b8c-4d1a-4baf-f49e-c1bf81684f14"},"execution_count":27,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Loss before: 0.8782154774250645\n","Loss after: 0.871893730342554\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"2VraQWsGssPU"},"source":["#5. Hessian & gradient descent"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"zMAvoHqissPU","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786954169245,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":5,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"dd53803d-d9d0-45cc-df26-819d695716e8"},"execution_count":29,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Hessian of f:\n","⎡2  3⎤\n","⎢    ⎥\n","⎣3  2⎦\n"]}],"source":["# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","# 🔹 5A. THE HESSIAN (matrix of second derivatives = curvature)\n","# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","\n","f5 = x_sym**2 + 3*x_sym*y_sym + y_sym**2\n","H = sp.hessian(f5, (x_sym, y_sym))\n","print('Hessian of f:')\n","sp.pprint(H)        # [[2, 3], [3, 2]]"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"d-pcpYFmssPU","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786954181322,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":7,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"247b657e-e643-492c-a5b4-6a33e094f1bb"},"execution_count":30,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Converged x: 3.998  (true minimum = 4)\n"]}],"source":["# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","# 🔹 5B. GRADIENT DESCENT ON A SIMPLE FUNCTION\n","# -----------------------------------------------------------\n","\n","# Minimise f(x) = (x - 4)**2, whose minimum is at x = 4.\n","# Update rule:  x <- x - lr * f'(x),  with f'(x) = 2*(x - 4)\n","xv = 0.0          # starting point\n","lr = 0.2\n","for step in range(15):\n","    grad = 2 * (xv - 4)        # the derivative\n","    xv = xv - lr * grad        # step against the gradient\n","print('Converged x:', round(xv, 3), ' (true minimum = 4)')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"KXgZJXpkssPU"},"source":["#### 🧪 LAB EXERCISE 5 — Hessian + gradient descent\n","\n","1. Compute the **Hessian** of `f = x**4 + y**2` with `sp.hessian`.\n","2. Run **gradient descent** to minimise `f(x) = (x - 7)**2`:\n","   start at `x = 0`, `lr = 0.1`, 20 steps, using `f'(x) = 2*(x - 